# Wenn du das Video mit KI erzeugen willst

Falls du ein KI-Video-Tool verwenden möchtest, kannst du es nicht sinnvoll als ein einziges 12-Minuten-Video generieren lassen. Besser: **Szene für Szene erzeugen** und dann schneiden.

## Genereller Prompt für jedes Szenen-Video

> Create a professional German IT training video in 720p, 16:9, 30 fps. The style is clean, educational, and suitable for an IHK exam presentation. Show a calm presenter in a modern training room or neutral studio background. Include OSI model slides, network diagrams, icons for HTTP, HTTPS, SMTP, TCP, UDP, IP, MAC, switches, routers, cables, fiber optics, and Wi-Fi. Use dark blue and orange color scheme. Add lower thirds with speaker names. No chaotic camera movement. Clear, structured, professional educational video.

## Szenenweise KI-Prompts

### Patrick Szene
> German IT presenter Patrick introduces the OSI model. Slide shows “OSI Model, 7 layers, ISO 1984”. Highlight Layer 7 Application Layer with browser, email, HTTP, HTTPS, SMTP icons. Professional, calm, 720p, educational style.

### Bastian Szene
> German IT presenter Bastian explains Layer 6 Presentation Layer and Layer 5 Session Layer. Show data formatting, JPEG, ASCII, TLS encryption lock, compression, session establishment between two computers. Clean slide animation, professional educational video.

### Issa Szene
> German IT presenter Issa explains Layer 4 Transport Layer and Layer 3 Network Layer. Show segmentation, TCP reliable transfer, UDP fast transfer, ports, IP packets, router routing path. Modern network diagram, 720p, educational style.

### Thomas Szene
> German IT presenter Thomas explains Layer 2 Data Link Layer and Layer 1 Physical Layer. Show switch, MAC addresses, Ethernet frames, copper cable, fiber optic light pulses, Wi-Fi radio waves, binary bits 0 and 1. Professional technical visualization.

### Bastian TCP/IP Szene
> Short comparison slide: OSI 7 layers versus TCP/IP 4 layers. Show mapping of OSI layers to TCP/IP layers. Text: “OSI = reference model, TCP/IP = practical Internet model.” Clean infographic style.

### Adem Szene
> German IT presenter Adem explains encapsulation in practice. Show HTTP request getting TCP header, IP header, MAC header, then converted to bits. Then show troubleshooting from Layer 1 to Layer 7: cable, MAC, IP, port, application. Calm, structured, professional conclusion.

